{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Committed `9906f0ec7b3`. All four acceptance criteria verified against the commit, not against notes.\n\n**AC1 — fixture re-derives.** `measure.py --check` → `OK: 1524 pairs ({'lexical': 1431, 'semantic': 93}) over 630 tickets re-derive exactly at cad39ed1289`.\n\n**AC2 — per-stratum recall, no pooled figure.** All four candidates re-run from the committed tree after the fixture refactor below; every number matches the ADR tables exactly:\n\n| candidate | lex@5 | lex@10 | sem@5 | sem@10 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| fts5 | 0.771 | 0.993 | 0.823 | 0.952 |\n| digest | 0.703 | 0.918 | 0.796 | 0.925 |\n| vector | 0.763 | 0.972 | 0.876 | 0.973 |\n| vector-raw | 0.765 | 0.977 | 0.839 | 0.946 |\n\n**AC3 — one architecture, justified from the semantic stratum.** ADR 0122 adopts the digest embedding at k=5. The recall table alone cannot carry that: a `--paired` exact-McNemar mode was added, and at k=5 semantic `vector` beats `fts5` distinguishably (p=0.0213) while `vector` vs `vector-raw` does not (p=0.0654). Both paired tables re-ran post-refactor and reproduce. Index path, freshness key, catch-up rule, embedding model, per-ticket cost and the bulk-duplicate artifact are all recorded.\n\n**AC4 — `gen_adr_index.py --check` rc=0, `check_adr_numbers.py` rc=0.**\n\n**Two defects caught before the commit.**\n\n1. The ADR cited `infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf:64-66` for the Bedrock allowlist and an \"operator-identity warning at :30-38\". The file is 26 lines. The allowlist is `:15-18` (statement `ConverseAnthropicClaudeOnly`, `:10`) and there is no operator-identity warning anywhere in it. Citation corrected, fabricated sentence deleted. The underlying constraint is real and load-bearing for the chosen architecture: both ARNs are `anthropic.claude-*`, so `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` would be denied, and adopting this ADR requires widening that list first.\n2. The draft commit message said the ADR \"selects fts5 at k=10\". It selects `vector` at k=5. Caught by reading the Decision section instead of trusting the draft.\n\n**The pre-commit large-file gate rejected the first commit attempt** — `benchmark.json` 8.0 MB and `digests.json` 884 KB against a 500 KB cap. Resolved without weakening the cap:\n\n- The fixture now carries only what AC1 enumerates (ids, aliases, titles, description heads, stratum). Full descriptions and digest inputs were never fixture data — `--build` rebuilds them from the store in the same pass, and `--check` re-derives from the store rather than trusting any stored copy. They moved to an uncommitted `corpus-text.json`, joining the Titan vector caches. `benchmark.json` is now 396 KB, under the cap with no exclusion.\n- `digests.json` (884 KB) is named in the existing `check-added-large-files` exclusion. That follows the documented precedent exactly — `uv.lock` and `.test_durations` are excluded there as \"committed, machine-generated files (~875 KB) … rather than raise the global cap for human-authored files\", and 884 KB is the same magnitude and the same rationale. It stays committed so the candidates reproduce without paying for 630 Bedrock calls. CI runs this hook with `--all-files`, so the exclusion is load-bearing there, not just locally; verified `pre-commit run check-added-large-files --all-files` rc=0.\n\n`file_impact` updated to the 8 paths actually committed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793504749560937195,"uuid":"b8642ca6-8d38-417c-8551-c677788b88ad"}